From db2283bdc4f25c2602df7c64d8685b4956f73dd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AliGram <aligram@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:14:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/67] fix(aligram): run refCountOf query on the DB worker
 thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 43630560041 (head f2b4393b): 8/64 tests failed, all in
AliGramRoomIntegrationTest, all IllegalStateException at line 260 —
refCountOf() called preservedBlobDao().getById() directly on the
Robolectric main-looper thread, which Room refuses ('Cannot access
database on the main thread'). Every other DAO call in the file
already runs via onDb()/onDbVoid(); refCountOf was the single
violation of the file's own rule. Fix routes its query through
onDb(); it is never called from inside another onDb() body, so no
deadlock on the single-thread executor. Test-only change; no
production code touched.
---
 .../ayugram/aligram/AliGramRoomIntegrationTest.java   | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/test/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramRoomIntegrationTest.java b/TMessagesProj/src/test/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramRoomIntegrationTest.java
index cec5e52d5..fe64fc7e4 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/test/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramRoomIntegrationTest.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/test/java/com/radolyn/ayugram/aligram/AliGramRoomIntegrationTest.java
@@ -256,8 +256,15 @@ public class AliGramRoomIntegrationTest {
         }
     }
 
-    private int refCountOf(String blobId) {
-        PreservedBlob blob = db.preservedBlobDao().getById(blobId);
+    // NOTE: this helper MUST run its query on the worker thread via onDb —
+    // the @Test methods run on the Robolectric main-looper thread and Room
+    // refuses DAO calls there ("Cannot access database on the main
+    // thread"). Calling getById() directly here failed all eight
+    // scenarios that assert refcounts (run 43630560041:
+    // IllegalStateException at line 260). It is never called from inside
+    // another onDb() body, so no deadlock on the single-thread executor.
+    private int refCountOf(String blobId) throws Exception {
+        PreservedBlob blob = onDb(() -> db.preservedBlobDao().getById(blobId));
         return blob == null ? -1 : blob.refCount;
     }
 
